  "sourceUnavailableStillWorksBody": "Your {library} novels and {downloaded} downloaded chapters are on this phone and are readable now, with or without {source}.",
  "@sourceUnavailableStillWorksBody": {
    "description": "⚠️ **The whole reason this screen exists.** SC-6's damage is not the failure — it is a reader concluding their library is gone. The three figures are LOCAL counts (B14, B48), so they are true without a network and they are the sentence that ends the fear."
  },
  "sourceUnavailableStillWorksEmpty": "Nothing is stored yet — and nothing was lost by this failure.",
  "@sourceUnavailableStillWorksEmpty": {
    "description": "⚠️ **A count of zero says \"nothing was lost\" rather than nothing.** The empty case and the failure case read alike otherwise, and a reader who has just seen a failure cannot tell \"empty\" from \"gone\"."
  },
